<html xmlns:o='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office' xmlns:w='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40'>
<head><meta charset='utf-8'><title>FL2024- exam 24</title>
<style>
body { font-family: Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; }
h1 { color: #C0392B; font-size: 20pt; }
h2 { color: #1F618D; font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 24px; }
.qtext { font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 8px; white-space: pre-wrap; }
.opt { margin: 4px 0 4px 20px; }
.correct { color: green; font-weight: bold; }
.selectedwrong { color: red; font-weight: bold; }
.selectedright { color: green; font-weight: bold; }
.explain { background: #F4F6F6; padding: 8px; margin-top: 8px; font-style: italic; }
.video { margin-top:6px; }
img { max-width: 500px; margin: 10px 0; display:block; }
</style></head><body><h1>FL2024- EXAM 24 - Ket qua &amp; giai thich</h1><p><b>Ho ten:</b> Hang Tran<br/><b>Ket qua:</b> 10/40<br/><b>Thoi gian lam bai:</b> 1 giờ 09 phút 49 giây<br/><b>Nop bai:</b> 2026-08-03T08:33:12.114Z</p><hr/><h2>Cau hoi 1</h2><div class="qtext">What benefits do static analysis tools have over test execution tools?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. A. Static analysis tools find defects earlier in the life cycle. [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. B. Static analysis tools can be used before code is written.</div><div class="opt ">c. C. Static analysis tools test that the delivered code meets business requirements.</div><div class="opt ">d. D. Static analysis tools are particularly effective for regression testing.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 3.1.2 Value của Static testing là tìm thấy lỗi sớm trước Dynamic test. B sai vì static analysis tool chủ yếu phân tích trên code. C sai vì "meets business requirements." là của Review. D sai vì "regression testing" là của Dynamic test</div><h2>Cau hoi 2</h2><div class="qtext">A system is designed to accept values of examination marks as follows: Fail :0-39 inclusive Pass :40-59 inclusive Merit :60-79 inclusive Distinction :80-100 inclusive In which of the following sets of values are all values in different equivalence partitions?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. A. 25, 40, 60, 75 [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. B. 0, 45, 79, 87 [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. C. 35, 40, 59, 69</div><div class="opt ">d. D. 25, 39, 60, 81</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.2, câu hỏi là xác định tất cả các giá trị test trong các phân vùng tương đương khác nhau</div><h2>Cau hoi 3</h2><div class="qtext">A washing machine has three temperature bands for different kinds of fabrics: fragile fabrics are washed at temperatures between 15 and 30 degrees Celsius; normal fabrics are washed at temperatures between 31 and 60 degrees Celsius; heavily soiled and tough fabrics are washed at temperatures between 61 and 100 degrees Celsius. Which of the following contains only values that are in different equivalence partitions?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. A. 15, 30, 60 [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. B. 20, 35, 60</div><div class="opt correct">c. C. 25, 45, 75 [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. D. 12, 35, 55</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.2.1 : Câu hỏi là đáp án nào chỉ chứa 1 giá trị trong các phân vùng tương đương khác nhau</div><h2>Cau hoi 4</h2><div class="qtext">Consider the following pseudo code: 1 Begin 2 Read Time 3 If Time &lt; 12 Then 4 Print(Time, "am") 5 Endif 6 If Time &gt; 12 Then 7 Print(Time −12, "pm") 8 Endif 9 If Time = 12 Then 10 Print (Time, "noon") 11 Endif 12 End How many test cases are needed to achieve 100 percent statement coverage?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. A. 1 [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. B. 2</div><div class="opt correct">c. C. 3 [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. D. 4</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.3, vẽ sơ đồ ra và xác định số test case để bao phủ 100% statement coverage</div><h2>Cau hoi 5</h2><div class="qtext">Consider the following pseudo code: 1 Begin 2 Read Time 3 If Time &lt; 12 Then 4 Print(Time, "am") 5 Endif 6 If Time &gt; 12 Then 7 Print(Time −12, "pm") 8 Endif 9 If Time = 12 Then 10 Print (Time, "noon") 11 Endif 12 End If the test cases Time = 11 and Time = 15 were input, what level of statement coverage would be achieved?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. A. 7/7 [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. B. 4/7</div><div class="opt ">c. C. 5/7</div><div class="opt correct">d. D. 6/7 [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.3 , vẽ sơ đồ ra và xác định 2 test case Time = 11 and Time = 15 đã bao phủ được bao nhiêu % decision coverage</div><h2>Cau hoi 6</h2><div class="qtext">A software component has the code shown below: Program BiggestA, Biggest: Integer Begin Read A Biggest = 10 While A &gt; 0 Do If A &gt; Biggest Then Biggest = A Endif Read A Enddo End The component has exit criteria for component testing that include 100% statement coverage. Which of the following test cases will satisfy this criterion?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. A. 0 [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. B. 10, 0</div><div class="opt ">c. C. 10, 5, 0</div><div class="opt correct">d. D. 10, 11, 0 [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.3 vẽ sơ đồ ra</div><h2>Cau hoi 7</h2><div class="qtext">Which option is part of the implementation and execution area of the fundamental test process?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Developing the tests. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. Comparing actual and expected results [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. Writing a test summary.</div><div class="opt ">d. Analysing lessons learnt for future releases.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 1.4 tìm ra B. A là của Design, C là của Monitoring, D là của Completion test</div><h2>Cau hoi 8</h2><div class="qtext">Which statement is most true?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. A.Different testing is needed depending upon the application. [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. B. All software is tested in the same way.</div><div class="opt ">c. C. A technique that finds defects will always find defects.</div><div class="opt ">d. D. A technique that has found no defects is not useful.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 1.3 nói về 7 nguyên lý test thì A là nguyên lý 6 Test phụ thuộc vào ngữ cảnh và phần mềm khác nhau. B sai All, C sai kỹ thuật tìm ra lỗi luôn luôn ( always) tìm ra lỗi là sai, D sai "kỹ thuật không tìm ra lỗi là không hữu ích"</div><h2>Cau hoi 9</h2><div class="qtext">A bug or defect is:</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. A. A mistake made by a person; [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. B. A run-time problem experienced by a user;</div><div class="opt correct">c. C. The result of an error or mistake; [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. D. The result of a failure, which may lead to an error?</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 1.2.3 sơ đồ Error- Defect- Failure thì tìm ra là C. Defect là kết quả của 1 error</div><h2>Cau hoi 10</h2><div class="qtext">What is retesting?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. A. Running the same test again in the same circumstances to reproduce the problem. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. B. A cursory run through a test pack to see if any new errors have been introduced.</div><div class="opt ">c. C. Checking that the predetermined exit criteria for the test phase have been met</div><div class="opt correct">d. D. Running a previously failed test against new software/data/documents to see if the problem is solved [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 2.2 Test types. D định nghĩa của "Confirmation testing ( Retest): confirm whether the original defect has been successfully fixed". A là định nghĩa của Regression test, C là định nghĩa của Exit criteria. A là chỉ hoạt động tái hiện lỗi Reproduce bug</div><h2>Cau hoi 11</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following is correct? Debugging is:</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. A. Testing/checking whether the software performs correctly. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. B. Checking that a previously reported defect has been corrected.</div><div class="opt correct">c. C. Identifying the cause of a defect, repairing the code and checking the fix is correct. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. D. Checking that no unintended consequences have occurred as a result of a fix.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 1.1.2 Debugging. D sai vì là định nghĩa của regression test, A là hoạt động test, B là retest</div><h2>Cau hoi 12</h2><div class="qtext">When is testing complete?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. A. When time and budget are exhausted. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. B. When there is enough information for sponsors to make an informed decision about release.</div><div class="opt correct">c. C. When there are no remaining high priority defects outstanding. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. D. When every data combination has been exercised successfully.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 5.1.3 Exit criteria thì C phù hợp là tiêu chí quan trọng nhất đánh giá hoàn thành "- (importance) Residual risks: issues/ open serious defect, untested"</div><h2>Cau hoi 13</h2><div class="qtext">Which list of levels of tester independence is in the correct order, starting with the most independent first?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. A. Tests designed by the author; tests designed by another member of the development team; tests designed by someone from a different company. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. B. Tests designed by someone from a different department within the company; tests designed by the author; tests designed by someone from a different company.</div><div class="opt correct">c. C. Tests designed by someone from a different company; tests designed by someone from a different department within the company; tests designed by another member of the development team. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. D. Tests designed by someone from a different department within the company; tests designed by someone from a different company; tests designed by the author.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 1.5.3 thứ tự của test independence đúng tứ mức độc lập cao nhất trở xuống, C là đúng nhất</div><h2>Cau hoi 14</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following is in the correct order (typically)?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. A. Unit testing, system testing, acceptance testing, maintenance testing. [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. B. System testing, unit testing, acceptance testing, maintenance testing.</div><div class="opt ">c. C. Acceptance testing, system testing, maintenance testing, unit testing.</div><div class="opt ">d. D. Unit testing, maintenance testing, system testing, acceptance testing.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 2.2 test levels. A là thứ tự đúng nhất</div><h2>Cau hoi 15</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following is not true of regression testing</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. A. It can be carried out at each stage of the life cycle. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. B. It serves to demonstrate that the changed software works as intended. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. C. It serves to demonstrate that software has not been unintentionally changed.</div><div class="opt ">d. D. It is often automated.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 2.2 Test types. Câu sai là B vì test cho " changed software" phần thay đổi của phần mềm là việc của New test, không phải của regression test. Regression test chạy lại test case ở những chỗ không thay đổi</div><h2>Cau hoi 16</h2><div class="qtext">One of the roles in a review is that of moderator, which of the following best describes this role?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. A. Plans the review, runs the review meeting and ensures that follow-up activities are completed. [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. B. Allocates time in the plan, decides which reviews will take place and that the benefits are delivered.</div><div class="opt ">c. C. Writes the document to be reviewed, agrees that the document can be reviewed, and updates the document with any changes.</div><div class="opt ">d. D. Documents all issues raised in the review meeting, records problems and open points.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 3.2.3 các vai trò của review. A là của Moderator còn gọi là Leader của review, B là của manager ra quyết định và cấp phép, C là của Author, D là Scribe</div><h2>Cau hoi 17</h2><div class="qtext">What do static analysis tools analyze?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. A. Design [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. B. Test cases</div><div class="opt ">c. C. Requirements</div><div class="opt correct">d. D. Program code [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 3.1.3 ba đáp án A,B,C sai là tài liệu chỉ có thể do Review tìm ra lỗi.</div><h2>Cau hoi 18</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following is most likely to be a benefit of using static techniques?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. A. Fewer performance defects. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. B. Productivity improvements in the development process. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. C. More efficient regression testing.</div><div class="opt ">d. D. Quick return on investment in static analysis tools.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 3.1.2 thì thấy B đúng, static test giúp cải thiện productivity, giảm thời gian và giảm chi phí. A,C là lỗi của dynamic, D là nhanh trả ra giá trị đầu tư là không có</div><h2>Cau hoi 19</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following are static techniques?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. A. Walkthrough. [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. B. State transition testing.</div><div class="opt ">c. C. Decision table testing.</div><div class="opt ">d. D. Statement testing.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 3.2.4 kỹ thuật static techniques không chạy source code là A. B,C,D sai vì là của Dynamic test</div><h2>Cau hoi 20</h2><div class="qtext">Which one of the following roles is typically used in a review?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. A. Champion. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. B. Author. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. C. Project sponsor.</div><div class="opt ">d. D. Custodian.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 3.2.3 Vai trò của review chỉ có B đúng</div><h2>Cau hoi 21</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following defines the expected result of a test?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. A. Test case [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. B. Test procedure</div><div class="opt ">c. C. Test execution schedule</div><div class="opt ">d. D. Test condition</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Glossary tra cứu định nghĩa Test case, có chứa thông tin về expected result của 1 cái test</div><h2>Cau hoi 22</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following describes structure-based (white-box) test case design techniques?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. A. Test cases are derived systematically from models of the system. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. B. Test cases are derived systematically from the tester's experience.</div><div class="opt correct">c. C. Test cases are derived systematically from the delivered code. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. D. Test cases are derived from the developers' experience.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.1.1 thì A là của Black box, B là Experience based, C là White box, D là Experience based</div><h2>Cau hoi 23</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following is a structure-based (white-box) technique?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. A. Decision table testing [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. B. State transition testing</div><div class="opt correct">c. C. Statement testing [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. D. Boundary value analysis</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.1.1 thì C đúng, A, B,D sai là vì của black box test</div><h2>Cau hoi 24</h2><div class="qtext">What can a risk-based approach to testing provide?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. A. The types of test techniques to be employed. [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. B. The total tests needed to provide 100 per cent coverage.</div><div class="opt ">c. C. An estimation of the total cost of development.</div><div class="opt ">d. D. Only that test execution is effective at reducing risk.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 5.2.3 thì A đúng Risk based giúp xác định test techniques. B sai vì 100% coverage là ko có, C sai là vì cost of development, D sai vì only</div><h2>Cau hoi 25</h2><div class="qtext">When assembling a test team to work on an enhancement to an existing system, which of the following has the highest level of test independence?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. A. A business analyst who wrote the original requirements for the system. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. B. A permanent programmer who reviewed some of the new code, but has not written any of it.</div><div class="opt ">c. C. A permanent tester who found most defects in the original system.</div><div class="opt correct">d. D. A contract tester who has never worked for the organization before. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer1.5.3 các mức độ độc lập thì D là cao nhất vì contract tester là thuê ngoài về</div><h2>Cau hoi 26</h2><div class="qtext">A new system is about to be developed. Which of the following functions has the highest level of risk?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. A. Likelihood of failure = 20%; impact value = $100,000 [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. B. Likelihood of failure = 10%; impact value = $150,000</div><div class="opt ">c. C. Likelihood of failure = 1%; impact value = $500,000</div><div class="opt ">d. D. Likelihood of failure = 2%; impact value = $200,000</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 5.2.1 cách tính Risk level = likelihood (probability) x Impact (harm) . Chỉ cần nhân đáp án vào là thấy A lớn nhất</div><h2>Cau hoi 27</h2><div class="qtext">Which pair of definitions is correct?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. A. Regression testing is checking that the reported defect has been fixed; retesting is testing that there are no additional problems in previously tested software. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. B. Regression testing is checking there are no additional problems in previously tested software; retesting enables developers to isolate the problem.</div><div class="opt ">c. C. Regression testing involves running all tests that have been run before; retesting runs new tests.</div><div class="opt correct">d. D. Regression testing is checking that there are no additional problems in previously tested software, retesting is demonstrating that the reported defect has been fixed. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 2.2 Test types. A sai cả 2 vế, B sai vế thứ 2 đanh định nghĩa debugging của lập trình, C sai vì all tests. Còn mỗi D đúng cả 2 vế</div><h2>Cau hoi 28</h2><div class="qtext">The following statements relate to activities that are part of the fundamental test process. i. Evaluating the testability of requirements. ii. Repeating testing activities after changes. iii. Designing the test environment set-up. iv. Developing and prioritizing test cases. v. Verifying the environment is set up correctly. Which statement below is TRUE?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. A. (i) and (ii) are part of analysis and design, (iii), (iv) and (v) are part of test implementation and execution. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. B. (i) and (iii) , (iv) are part of analysis and design, (ii) and (v) are part of test implementation and execution. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. C. (i) and (v) are part of analysis and design, (ii), (iii) and (iv) are part of test implementation and execution.</div><div class="opt ">d. D. (i) and (iv) are part of analysis and design, (ii), (iii) and (v) are part of test implementation and execution.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 1.4.1</div><h2>Cau hoi 29</h2><div class="qtext">Which statement correctly describes the public and profession aspects of the code of ethics?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. A. Public: Certified software testers shall act in the best interests of their client and employer (being consistent with the wider public interest). Profession: Certified software testers shall advance the integrity and reputation of their industry consistent with the public interest. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. B. Public: Certified software testers shall advance the integrity and reputation of the profession consistent with the public interest. Profession: Certified software testers shall consider the wider public interest in their actions.</div><div class="opt ">c. C. Public: Certified software testers shall consider the wider public interest in their actions. Profession: Certified software testers shall participate in lifelong learning regarding the practice of their profession and shall promote an ethical approach to the practice of their profession.</div><div class="opt correct">d. D. Public: Certified software testers shall consider the wider public interest in their actions. Profession: Certified software testers shall advance the integrity and reputation of their industry consistent with the public interest. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Theo 1 tài liệu trên mạng chúng tôi đọc đc thì "the code of ethics" được coi là 1 "set of rules or regulary about good and bad behavior" cần phải được tuân thủ theo khi phát triển và test phần mềm ( confidential information là 1 ví dụ rất rõ về cái này) , các rules này xuất phát từ nhiều nguồn khác nhau: The benefit and interest of public (consider act in the interest of public là xem xét đến các mối quan tâm của cộng đồng), Professional ( tester should follow the set of values, principles, standards and advance the integrity of their profession tester nên tuân theo các rules, standards, principles mà team đưa ra để đảm bảo tính toàn vẹn và chuyên nghiệp)</div><h2>Cau hoi 30</h2><div class="qtext">A top-down development strategy affects which level of testing most?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. A. Component testing [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. B. Integration testing [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. C. System testing</div><div class="opt ">d. D. User acceptance testing</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 2.2 test level.</div><h2>Cau hoi 31</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following is a non-functional requirement?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. A. The system will enable users to buy books. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. B. The system will allow users to return books.</div><div class="opt ">c. C. The system will ensure security of the customer details.</div><div class="opt correct">d. D. The system will allow up to 100 users to log in at the same time. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 2.2 test type. Chú ý mọi người hay nhầm đáp án C "ensure security of the customer details." là 1 yêu cầu về non-functional nhưng đọc như vậy là sai. C là 1 các yêu cầu về functional về security giống như các tính năng Login, phân quyền gọi là các tính năng về security. Còn các yêu cầu non-function về security là các yêu cầu Protect data ( nói chung ko nói về tính năng cụ thể mà các yêu cầu chung cho toàn hệ thống để bảo đảm an toàn)</div><h2>Cau hoi 32</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following statements are true? (i) For every development activity there is a corresponding testing activity. (ii) Each test level has the same test objectives. (iii) The analysis and design of tests for a given test level should begin after the corresponding development activity. (iv)Testers should be involved in reviewing documents as soon as drafts are available in the development life cycle.</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. A. (i) and (ii) [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. B. (iii) and (iv)</div><div class="opt ">c. C. (ii) and (iii)</div><div class="opt correct">d. D. (i) and (iv) [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 2.1.2 goog testing ( học thuộc) ii sai vì "the same test objectives". iii sai vì "begin after the corresponding development activity"</div><h2>Cau hoi 33</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following statements are correct for walkthroughs? (i) Often led by the author. (ii) Documented and defined results. (iii) All participants have defined roles. (iv) Used to aid learning. (v) Main purpose is to find defects.</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. A. (i) and (v) are correct. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. B. (ii) and (iii) are correct.</div><div class="opt correct">c. C. (i) and (iv) are correct. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. D. (iii) and (iv) are correct</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 3.2.4 Review types thì walkthough có (i) lead by author và (iv) để training. và ii, iii, v là đặc điểm của inspection</div><h2>Cau hoi 34</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following has the typical formal review activities in the correct sequence?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. A. Kick-off, review meeting, planning, follow-up. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. B. Kick-off, planning, review meeting, re-work.</div><div class="opt correct">c. C. Planning, kick-off, individual preparation, review meeting. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. D. Planning, individual preparation, follow-up, re-work</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 3.2.2 review process</div><h2>Cau hoi 35</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following statements are true? (i) Defects are likely to be found earlier in the development process by using reviews rather than static analysis. (ii) Walkthroughs require code but static analysis does not require code. (iii) Informal reviews can be performed on code and specifications. (iv) Dynamic techniques are generally used before static techniques. (v) Dynamic techniques can only be used after code is ready to be executed.</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. A. (i), (ii), (vi). [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. B. (ii), (iii), (v).</div><div class="opt ">c. C. (i), (iv), (v).</div><div class="opt correct">d. D. (i), (iii), (v). [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 3.1.2 và loại trừ ii sai vì walkthrough là hình thức reiview không thay đc tool phân tích code ( review ko hết đc code). iv sai vì dynamic chạy trước static</div><h2>Cau hoi 36</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following is most likely to be performed by developers?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. A. Technical review of a functional specification. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. B. Walkthrough of a requirements document.</div><div class="opt ">c. C. Informal review of a program specification.</div><div class="opt correct">d. D. Static analysis of a software model. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 6.1 A,B,C là tester tham gia đc, D là tool phân tích tĩnh chỉ dùng cho lập trình viên</div><h2>Cau hoi 37</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following are most characteristic of structure-based testing? (i) Information about how the software is constructed is used to derive test cases. (ii) Statement coverage and/or decision coverage can be measured for existing test cases. (iii) The knowledge and experience of people are used to derive test cases. (iv) Test cases are derived from a model or specification of the system</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. A. (i) and (ii) [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. B. (ii) and (iii)</div><div class="opt ">c. C. (ii) and (iv)</div><div class="opt ">d. D. (i) and (iii)</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.1.1 chọn i và ii của white box test và loại trừ, iii là của experience based, iv là của black box</div><h2>Cau hoi 38</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following are valid justifications for developers testing their own code during unit testing? (i) Their lack of independence is mitigated by independent testing during system and acceptance testing. (ii)A person with a good understanding of the code can find more defects more quickly using white-box techniques. (iii)Developers have a better understanding of the requirements than testers. (iv)Testers write unnecessary incident reports because they find minor differences between the way in which the system behaves and the way in which it is specified to work.</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. A. (i) and (ii) [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. B. (i) and (iv)</div><div class="opt ">c. C. (ii) and (iii)</div><div class="opt ">d. D. (iii) and (iv)</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 1.5.3 câu hỏi là giải thích về việc developer thực hiện unit test trên code của anh ta thì là i đúng vì thiếu độc lập ( khách quan) nên cần phải có tester độc lập test ở phase sau, ii đúng vì developer hiểu biết về code, tìm lỗi và sửa lỗi nhanh hơn. iii sai vì developer không thể hiểu requirement hơn tester độc lập, iv sai vì "unnecessary incident reports"</div><h2>Cau hoi 39</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following pairs of test tools are likely to be most useful during the test analysis and design stage of the fundamental test process? (i) Test execution tool (ii) Test data preparation tool (iii) Test management tool (iv) Requirements management tool</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. A. (i) and (ii) [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. B. (i) and (iv)</div><div class="opt ">c. C. (ii) and (iii)</div><div class="opt correct">d. D. (iii) and (iv) [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 6.1 nói chung giai đoạn analysis and design chủ yếu dùng tool để quản lý task, test case, test document, requirement</div><h2>Cau hoi 40</h2><div class="qtext">What is regression test?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. A. Running the same test again in the same circumstances to reproduce the problem. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. B. A cursory run through a test pack to see if any new errors have been introduced. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. C. Checking that the predetermined exit criteria for the test phase have been met</div><div class="opt ">d. D. Running a previously failed test against new software/data/documents to see if the problem is solved</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 2.2.3 Test types. định nghĩa của Regression test là "Regression testing: re-run tests to detect any introduced issues". D là định nghĩa của Retest, C là định nghĩa của Exit criteria. A là chỉ hoạt động tái hiện lỗi Reproduce bug</div></body></html>